   $q$Which sentence would best replace sentence 14 as a conclusion that shows how the narrator changed?$q$, $q$[{"text":"On the walk back, I counted a flock of geese overhead in fives without even thinking.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Bird counts help scientists learn how bird populations change over time.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"generic-fact-ending"},{"text":"Aunt Marisol and I went to Willow Marsh to count birds on a cold morning.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"restates-situation"},{"text":"We drove home after the count, and I took a long nap on the couch.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"flat-ending-no-reflection"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$On the walk back, I counted a flock of geese overhead in fives without even thinking.$q$, $q$The correct choice shows the narrator using the new trick on her own, which proves the narrator has changed since sentence 7. The fact about scientists is tempting, but it ends the story with information instead of the narrator's experience.$q$, 'draft', '30ffdc0e-3d8d-5c9c-beba-8d0ce8ee1dc7')
