   $q$The writer wants sentence 7 to show how much time passes. Which revision does this best?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Mr. Nakamura will watch me struggle with the clay on the wheel.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-tense"},{"text":"Mr. Nakamura watched me, and then he watched me some more.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"vague-repetition"},{"text":"Mr. Nakamura, who has taught art at our school, watched me struggle.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"adds-unrelated-detail"},{"text":"For almost ten minutes, Mr. Nakamura watched me struggle without saying a word.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$For almost ten minutes, Mr. Nakamura watched me struggle without saying a word.$q$, $q$"For almost ten minutes" tells the reader exactly how long the struggle lasts. The choice with "will watch" changes the tense, which confuses the order of events in a story told in the past.$q$, 'draft', '01a7b91b-2371-5f77-a4e9-ecf6f09af0f4')
