   $q$Sentences 7 and 8 follow the same pattern. What is the best reason for the writer to keep them?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The sentences make the narrative longer, and longer stories are always better.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"length-equals-quality"},{"text":"The sentences show that the bug in the game has already been solved.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-sequence"},{"text":"The repeated pattern shows the narrator checking step by step and builds frustration.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The sentences give the reader new facts about how bananas grow in a jungle.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-purpose"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The repeated pattern shows the narrator checking step by step and builds frustration.$q$, $q$The matching pattern shows each failed check, so the reader feels the narrator's growing frustration. The bug is not solved until sentence 12, so the choice saying it is already solved misreads the order of events.$q$, 'draft', 'abfeb509-6855-58a7-b951-aa4c79fa3520')
